1
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:12,040
So you're going home?
Your husband isn't trying to stop you?

2
00:03:12,120 --> 00:03:13,320
I'll serve it for you, Grandpa.

3
00:03:13,400 --> 00:03:14,640
No need.

4
00:03:14,720 --> 00:03:17,040
I already drink a tonic every day.

5
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:22,320
Before Hathaya left,
she bought the herbs and asked the maid

6
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:24,120
to prepare them for me every day.

7
00:03:24,200 --> 00:03:25,160
Be patient, sweetheart.

8
00:03:26,480 --> 00:03:29,160
PREVIOUSLY

9
00:03:29,240 --> 00:03:30,600
Grandma!

10
00:03:43,000 --> 00:03:44,800
May the sacred spirits

11
00:03:44,880 --> 00:03:48,600
and guardian deities of this place

12
00:03:49,800 --> 00:03:54,160
protect my grandmother and keep her safe.

13
00:03:55,080 --> 00:03:56,520
Please let her…

14
00:03:58,040 --> 00:04:00,960
recover quickly. Please guide the doctors…

15
00:04:02,280 --> 00:04:06,360
so they can heal her
and make her strong again.

16
00:04:10,800 --> 00:04:13,080
May all the good deeds I have done

17
00:04:13,160 --> 00:04:16,839
in past lives and in this life

18
00:04:18,240 --> 00:04:22,000
bring merit to my grandmother.

19
00:04:23,200 --> 00:04:26,600
Please let her live
and regain her strength.

20
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:56,360
Grandma Duangjai is a good person
who has always thought and done good.

21
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:04,320
May the guardian spirits protect

22
00:05:04,920 --> 00:05:06,840
the life of such a good person.

23
00:05:07,440 --> 00:05:09,360
Sadhu.

24
00:05:29,520 --> 00:05:30,560
Here.

25
00:05:31,600 --> 00:05:32,560
Food.

26
00:05:33,080 --> 00:05:35,480
I can't eat. You take it.

27
00:05:36,160 --> 00:05:38,400
Take it.

28
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:39,560
Here's some water too.

29
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:47,400
When your grandma gets better,

30
00:05:48,280 --> 00:05:52,040
she'll need someone to take care of her.
If you get sick,

31
00:05:52,680 --> 00:05:54,080
who's going to look after her?

32
00:05:55,520 --> 00:05:56,640
Eat.

33
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:09,040
Come on.

34
00:06:09,840 --> 00:06:12,640
I know you want to stay
close to your grandma,

35
00:06:13,280 --> 00:06:14,640
but no need to eat so fast.

36
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:19,840
Slow down, or you'll choke.
We barely have doctors here. Slow down.

37
00:06:22,920 --> 00:06:24,040
Earlier,

38
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:27,200
when you were praying,

39
00:06:27,960 --> 00:06:32,400
you said my grandma is a good person
who thinks and does good.

40
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,840
How do you know what she's like?

41
00:06:38,120 --> 00:06:39,200
I've met her before.

42
00:06:41,680 --> 00:06:43,280
You know my grandma?

43
00:06:46,240 --> 00:06:48,760
How come I never knew about this?

44
00:06:50,160 --> 00:06:53,440
I want to know
who Hathaya's mother is living with

45
00:06:53,520 --> 00:06:55,680
and whether her grandmother
is really sick.

46
00:07:01,360 --> 00:07:02,360
Here, Grandma.

47
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:04,920
Use this as capital for your stall

48
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:06,880
so you won't have to borrow from anyone.

49
00:07:08,120 --> 00:07:10,560
Well, it was a secret.

50
00:07:11,480 --> 00:07:14,680
Mr. Pichai ordered me
to investigate your situation.

51
00:07:14,760 --> 00:07:18,880
That's how he learned you weren't lying
and that everything you said was true.

52
00:07:24,720 --> 00:07:25,800
Thank you.

53
00:07:27,840 --> 00:07:28,960
You're…

54
00:07:31,080 --> 00:07:32,480
not angry

55
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:36,960
that I was investigating you?

56
00:07:41,320 --> 00:07:44,600
At least now I know Grandpa
doesn't hate me.

57
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:50,040
And Grandpa knows everything
I told him was true.

58
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:53,000
Listen to me.

59
00:07:53,720 --> 00:07:56,480
Mr. Pichai cares about you.

60
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:59,840
Otherwise, he never would've sent me
to investigate your situation.

61
00:08:07,480 --> 00:08:08,720
We have to share the water.
There's only one bottle.

62
00:08:31,440 --> 00:08:34,080
Doctor, the patient's pulse is dropping.

63
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:42,799
Is the doctor here yet?
Patient in critical condition.

64
00:08:42,880 --> 00:08:44,120
RECORDING IS PROHIBITED

65
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:46,160
Have the doctor
come immediately once finished.

66
00:08:47,040 --> 00:08:49,480
Nurse, is the doctor here yet?

67
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:53,640
The doctor is in surgery right now.
The doctor will come as soon as possible.

68
00:08:56,160 --> 00:08:58,480
We have to transfer your grandma
to a private hospital.

69
00:08:58,560 --> 00:09:00,880
No. I can't let you do that for me.

70
00:09:05,960 --> 00:09:09,360
She has to be transferred.
That's an order.

71
00:09:11,640 --> 00:09:12,520
Grandpa.

72
00:09:13,160 --> 00:09:18,200
Transfer her now. Take her to
a private hospital with proper equipment.

73
00:09:19,200 --> 00:09:20,840
I'll cover all the expenses.

74
00:09:23,320 --> 00:09:24,600
Yes, Grandpa.

75
00:09:25,360 --> 00:09:27,600
Nurse.

76
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:03,560
Doctor, how is my grandmother?

77
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:06,600
She was brought in just in time.

78
00:10:06,680 --> 00:10:08,120
She's safe now.

79
00:10:08,200 --> 00:10:12,320
After she rests and recovers here
for a bit, she should be able to go home.

80
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:14,640
Thank you so much, Doctor.

81
00:10:14,720 --> 00:10:15,720
You're welcome.

82
00:10:31,440 --> 00:10:32,720
Grandpa,

83
00:10:33,600 --> 00:10:35,360
Grandma is safe now.

84
00:10:42,840 --> 00:10:47,040
Grandpa, thank you so much
for saving Grandma.

85
00:10:47,120 --> 00:10:50,640
If you hadn't helped her, I don't know
what would have happened to her.

86
00:10:50,720 --> 00:10:52,680
Thank you so much, Grandpa.

87
00:10:52,760 --> 00:10:54,600
All right.

88
00:10:54,680 --> 00:10:56,760
Get up, Hathaya.

89
00:10:59,640 --> 00:11:02,360
Hathaya. I said get up.

90
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:07,680
You don't have to thank me.

91
00:11:08,520 --> 00:11:12,960
After all, Duangjai was once
my son's mother-in-law.

92
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:16,240
The person you should thank is over there.

93
00:11:17,320 --> 00:11:18,240
Ramil.

94
00:11:24,040 --> 00:11:24,920
RAMIL

95
00:11:29,960 --> 00:11:30,840
Hello?

96
00:11:33,680 --> 00:11:36,120
Hathaya's grandmother
is in critical condition, sir.

97
00:11:37,040 --> 00:11:40,240
This hospital doesn't have
enough equipment or staff.

98
00:11:41,640 --> 00:11:43,280
Sir, could you please

99
00:11:44,840 --> 00:11:46,120
help Hathaya?

100
00:11:51,200 --> 00:11:53,400
He asked me to come help you.

101
00:12:04,360 --> 00:12:08,880
All right. Now that your grandmother
is safe, you can relax.

102
00:12:10,200 --> 00:12:13,440
Now tell me, which hotel should I stay at?

103
00:12:14,480 --> 00:12:16,400
You're not going back
to Bangkok yet, Grandpa?

104
00:12:17,480 --> 00:12:18,880
I still have some work to do.

105
00:12:22,720 --> 00:12:26,200
If you know somewhere
I could stay, tell Ramil.

106
00:12:28,680 --> 00:12:30,000
Yes, sir.

107
00:12:30,800 --> 00:12:31,760
Grandpa.

108
00:12:33,560 --> 00:12:36,160
Thank you again so much.

109
00:12:36,240 --> 00:12:39,400
I already told you not to thank me.

110
00:12:39,480 --> 00:12:43,400
I'm a businessman.
I never help anyone for free.

111
00:12:44,920 --> 00:12:46,800
I only do good expecting something back.

112
00:13:09,080 --> 00:13:10,160
So,

113
00:13:11,480 --> 00:13:14,600
once you think of a hotel for Mr. Pichai…

114
00:13:18,920 --> 00:13:20,600
send me the location.

115
00:13:27,680 --> 00:13:33,200
I'm going to go take care
of Mr. Pichai now.

116
00:14:05,680 --> 00:14:06,640
Oh.

117
00:14:07,200 --> 00:14:08,400
Has Father come downstairs yet?

118
00:14:08,480 --> 00:14:10,920
Mr. Pichai already came down and ate.

119
00:14:11,520 --> 00:14:13,840
Then where did Father go?

120
00:14:13,920 --> 00:14:15,280
I don't know.

121
00:14:16,160 --> 00:14:17,160
Well…

122
00:14:17,240 --> 00:14:18,720
Did he go to the development?

123
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:20,120
I don't know.

124
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:22,280
You don't know anything I ask.

125
00:14:22,360 --> 00:14:24,120
Why do I even pay you?

126
00:14:24,200 --> 00:14:28,120
My job is to take care of the food
and keep the house clean.

127
00:14:28,720 --> 00:14:32,000
I'm sorry, but I'm not his secretary.

128
00:14:32,600 --> 00:14:36,400
You are his close family, and even you
don't know where Mr. Pichai went.

129
00:14:36,480 --> 00:14:38,840
I'm only a maid. How would I know?

130
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:40,960
Watch your mouth.

131
00:14:41,600 --> 00:14:44,440
I've wanted to throw you out
of this house for a long time.

132
00:14:44,520 --> 00:14:47,720
You're only lucky
Father keeps protecting you.

133
00:14:48,440 --> 00:14:49,560
But watch yourself.

134
00:14:49,640 --> 00:14:52,920
The day Father is no longer here
to protect you,

135
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:56,240
I'll be the first one
to throw you out of this house.

136
00:14:56,320 --> 00:14:58,000
Understood.

137
00:15:00,880 --> 00:15:03,000
God, I hate her.

138
00:15:03,720 --> 00:15:04,960
Mom,

139
00:15:05,040 --> 00:15:08,840
don't waste your time
on servants and parasites.

140
00:15:08,920 --> 00:15:11,520
Grandpa probably went to the office
like he does every day.

141
00:15:11,600 --> 00:15:13,480
Then let's hurry to work

142
00:15:13,560 --> 00:15:16,400
and make ourselves useful to Grandpa.

143
00:15:16,480 --> 00:15:17,880
Okay, Mom.

144
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:21,600
I'll stop at a famous restaurant
and pick up lunch for Grandpa too.

145
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:35,000
Grandma.

146
00:15:41,760 --> 00:15:43,720
My angel.

147
00:15:44,720 --> 00:15:47,040
You're safe now, Grandma.

148
00:15:47,680 --> 00:15:50,200
I thought I was dead.

149
00:15:53,880 --> 00:15:56,400
What about those two?

150
00:15:57,160 --> 00:16:00,000
They've been arrested
and sent to jail, right?

151
00:16:00,600 --> 00:16:04,320
Mom and her new husband got away.

152
00:16:04,920 --> 00:16:06,680
The police are still looking for them.

153
00:16:08,120 --> 00:16:10,280
People as evil as them

154
00:16:10,360 --> 00:16:13,160
deserve whatever karma comes their way.

155
00:16:20,440 --> 00:16:23,680
Wow. This place
is as luxurious as a hotel.

156
00:16:24,320 --> 00:16:27,480
Where did you get the money for this?
Take me home, sweetheart.

157
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:29,600
No, Grandma.

158
00:16:29,680 --> 00:16:33,760
You need to stay here and recover first.
You still need wound care too.

159
00:16:34,640 --> 00:16:37,720
No. Take me home.

160
00:16:38,320 --> 00:16:40,440
You'll have to struggle

161
00:16:40,520 --> 00:16:44,200
to find money for my treatment again.
I don't want that.

162
00:16:44,800 --> 00:16:47,680
A kind person is paying for all of it.

163
00:16:48,280 --> 00:16:49,320
Who?

164
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:53,400
What a generous soul.

165
00:16:53,480 --> 00:16:56,160
Grandpa. My grandpa.

166
00:16:56,960 --> 00:16:58,200
What?

167
00:16:58,280 --> 00:16:59,880
Your grandpa came here?

168
00:17:00,480 --> 00:17:01,400
Yes.

169
00:17:02,920 --> 00:17:07,319
Ramil called Grandpa,
and he came down right away.

170
00:17:07,400 --> 00:17:10,800
If it weren't for him, we never
would've been able to transfer you here.

171
00:17:15,200 --> 00:17:18,119
One second, Grandma. Let me answer this.

172
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:23,400
Yes?

173
00:17:25,960 --> 00:17:29,840
Is Grandpa going to rest at the hotel,
or are you taking him sightseeing?

174
00:17:31,320 --> 00:17:33,080
Mr. Pichai is at the government hospital.

175
00:17:33,680 --> 00:17:34,920
What?

176
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:37,480
Why did Grandpa go back there?

177
00:17:37,560 --> 00:17:40,320
Mr. Pichai wants you to come here.
Right away.

178
00:17:40,400 --> 00:17:42,440
Okay. I'll hurry over.

179
00:17:47,280 --> 00:17:50,720
Grandma, Grandpa wants to see me.
I have to go.

180
00:17:50,800 --> 00:17:54,120
Then hurry. Don't keep him waiting.

181
00:17:54,200 --> 00:17:55,040
Go.

182
00:17:55,120 --> 00:17:57,400
I'll be back as soon as I can.
You stay here and rest.

183
00:17:57,480 --> 00:17:58,440
All right.

184
00:17:58,520 --> 00:18:00,040
And don't be stubborn.

185
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:02,360
Seriously, you're always stubborn.

186
00:18:02,440 --> 00:18:05,360
All right. I'll stay right here.
Come back soon.

187
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:07,640
Okay. Lie down and rest.

188
00:18:08,320 --> 00:18:09,880
Don't run away.

189
00:18:19,560 --> 00:18:21,280
Ramil, where's Grandpa?

190
00:18:24,800 --> 00:18:27,560
Go in. Mr. Pichai is waiting for you.

191
00:18:29,080 --> 00:18:30,160
Go on.

192
00:18:35,320 --> 00:18:36,560
There she is.

193
00:18:37,200 --> 00:18:39,320
I understand

194
00:18:39,400 --> 00:18:40,920
that government hospitals

195
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:43,800
are constantly dealing
with budget shortages,

196
00:18:44,600 --> 00:18:47,400
especially small hospitals
near the border like this one.

197
00:18:48,240 --> 00:18:50,240
So I would like

198
00:18:50,320 --> 00:18:52,960
to donate ten million baht.

199
00:18:58,240 --> 00:19:02,040
You will present this donation
on behalf of your father.

200
00:19:15,960 --> 00:19:17,000
Hold on.

201
00:19:17,960 --> 00:19:19,160
Let me take a picture.

202
00:19:21,040 --> 00:19:23,240
One, two, three.

203
00:19:23,320 --> 00:19:26,240
One, two, three.

204
00:19:29,600 --> 00:19:31,880
Thank you so much, Grandpa.

205
00:19:32,920 --> 00:19:34,080
Why are you thanking me?

206
00:19:35,280 --> 00:19:37,240
I was born and raised here.

207
00:19:37,320 --> 00:19:40,840
I want to thank you
on behalf of everyone here.

208
00:19:42,200 --> 00:19:44,160
Burapha was my son.

209
00:19:44,680 --> 00:19:46,520
I wanted to make merit

210
00:19:46,600 --> 00:19:49,680
and dedicate it to him.

211
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:55,480
None of us choose where we're born.
Life isn't a level playing field.

212
00:19:56,760 --> 00:20:00,080
I was fortunate.
I worked hard and made money.

213
00:20:00,160 --> 00:20:04,960
When I get sick, I can afford
top hospitals and skilled doctors.

214
00:20:05,680 --> 00:20:07,680
But here, there aren't
enough doctors or nurses.

215
00:20:08,880 --> 00:20:10,440
The facilities aren't adequate.

216
00:20:11,040 --> 00:20:13,000
When patients' relatives come to visit,

217
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:17,160
they end up sleeping on the floor
or wherever they can find space.

218
00:20:18,000 --> 00:20:21,320
We call ourselves
a developed country with 5G,

219
00:20:21,880 --> 00:20:23,800
but the quality of life
for ordinary people

220
00:20:24,640 --> 00:20:27,080
is no different from that
of an underdeveloped country.

221
00:20:28,480 --> 00:20:30,320
Like this hospital.

222
00:20:30,920 --> 00:20:33,520
That's why I want to help
as much as I can.

223
00:20:34,240 --> 00:20:36,200
But it still isn't enough.
It isn't sustainable.

224
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:40,080
It's only temporary.

225
00:20:40,920 --> 00:20:43,320
The best way to create real,

226
00:20:43,960 --> 00:20:47,600
lasting change is to get rid

227
00:20:48,160 --> 00:20:50,800
of corrupt government officials.

228
00:20:52,840 --> 00:20:56,600
Those people are parasites.
They're the real blight on society.

229
00:20:57,240 --> 00:20:58,160
It makes me angry.

230
00:20:59,080 --> 00:21:01,120
Mr. Pichai, are you ready to go back?

231
00:21:03,560 --> 00:21:04,640
You're coming back too.

232
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:08,760
Why do you want me to go back?

233
00:21:08,840 --> 00:21:11,120
Well, to work.

234
00:21:11,840 --> 00:21:13,920
You'll repay what I spent
on your grandma's care.

235
00:21:35,960 --> 00:21:39,520
Okay. I'll go back
and work for you, Grandpa.

236
00:21:48,680 --> 00:21:50,400
You're back, sweetheart?

237
00:21:52,960 --> 00:21:53,880
Sir…

238
00:22:01,040 --> 00:22:02,520
I came to visit.

239
00:22:04,400 --> 00:22:07,960
Thank you so much for helping me.

240
00:22:08,600 --> 00:22:11,920
If it weren't for you, I might have died.

241
00:22:13,400 --> 00:22:17,640
Please don't say that. Truthfully,
I had a responsibility to help.

242
00:22:17,720 --> 00:22:21,840
After all, you were
my son's mother-in-law.

243
00:22:22,640 --> 00:22:25,440
I was a terrible mother-in-law.

244
00:22:25,520 --> 00:22:28,240
I never had the chance
to take care of my son-in-law.

245
00:22:28,320 --> 00:22:29,920
And my daughter behaved so badly

246
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:33,760
that she caused trouble for your family.

247
00:22:33,840 --> 00:22:35,920
I'm truly sorry.

248
00:22:36,760 --> 00:22:39,240
Let it go. It's all in the past.

249
00:22:39,880 --> 00:22:43,560
And you weren't the one at fault.
Your daughter was.

250
00:22:44,600 --> 00:22:47,680
I can't avoid responsibility.

251
00:22:47,760 --> 00:22:50,960
When a child turns out badly,
the parents have to share the blame.

252
00:22:52,040 --> 00:22:53,680
You're right.

253
00:22:54,720 --> 00:22:57,400
Parents can't simply wash their hands
of responsibility.

254
00:23:00,920 --> 00:23:03,640
I'd like Hathaya to come work for me.

255
00:23:04,360 --> 00:23:05,520
Would you be fine with that?

256
00:23:12,880 --> 00:23:15,000
May I ask you something?

257
00:23:18,600 --> 00:23:20,360
Do you still love your granddaughter?

258
00:23:23,960 --> 00:23:28,320
If you don't love her, please don't take
her back there just to make her suffer.

259
00:23:29,280 --> 00:23:33,920
It's not because I'm selfish
and want her here taking care of me.

260
00:23:34,640 --> 00:23:37,560
I just don't want her to suffer anymore.

261
00:23:39,160 --> 00:23:43,280
All this time,
she's done everything for other people.

262
00:23:44,360 --> 00:23:47,080
She sacrificed her own happiness

263
00:23:47,160 --> 00:23:49,600
for me and for her mother.

264
00:23:51,400 --> 00:23:54,960
I want her to have
a life of her own for once.

265
00:23:56,360 --> 00:23:58,880
I want my granddaughter to be happy.

266
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:06,960
You can put your mind at ease.

267
00:24:08,480 --> 00:24:13,200
I'll treat Hathaya well.
I'll take care of her. I'll protect her.

268
00:24:14,200 --> 00:24:16,080
Hathaya is my granddaughter.

269
00:24:19,120 --> 00:24:20,120
Thank you.

270
00:24:21,320 --> 00:24:23,640
Please take care of her for me.

271
00:24:53,680 --> 00:24:55,560
Where has Father gone?

272
00:24:55,640 --> 00:24:58,120
He didn't go to the office,
and he won't answer his phone.

273
00:24:58,720 --> 00:25:01,640
I sent Grandpa hundreds of messages.

274
00:25:01,720 --> 00:25:03,360
He hasn't read any of them.

275
00:25:04,160 --> 00:25:06,400
Something isn't right.

276
00:25:07,160 --> 00:25:08,960
What if something happened to him?

277
00:25:09,040 --> 00:25:11,600
I'm not waiting any longer.
I'm going to report him missing.

278
00:25:12,880 --> 00:25:16,400
I'm worried too, Mom. Let's go.

279
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:21,160
Father.

280
00:25:23,400 --> 00:25:24,880
Father.

281
00:25:24,960 --> 00:25:27,080
Where have you been?

282
00:25:27,160 --> 00:25:30,680
We missed you so much.

283
00:25:32,520 --> 00:25:33,720
Grandpa.

284
00:25:33,800 --> 00:25:35,920
I missed you so much, Grandpa.

285
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:38,400
You were so mean
for not answering my messages.

286
00:25:39,320 --> 00:25:41,520
I had business to handle
and wanted some peace and quiet,

287
00:25:41,600 --> 00:25:44,880
so I turned my phone off.
I just turned it back on.

288
00:25:46,320 --> 00:25:48,920
Are you still angry with me?

289
00:25:49,000 --> 00:25:51,320
I love you and miss you so much.

290
00:25:52,680 --> 00:25:54,040
I missed you too.

291
00:25:54,120 --> 00:25:56,160
Where did you go, Father?

292
00:26:00,200 --> 00:26:02,520
Hathaya, you--

293
00:26:03,800 --> 00:26:04,960
Why did you come back?

294
00:26:07,040 --> 00:26:09,280
Grandpa, why did you bring Hathaya here?

295
00:26:10,520 --> 00:26:14,400
I went to Hathaya's hometown
and spent some time there.

296
00:26:16,400 --> 00:26:18,600
All right. Father,

297
00:26:18,680 --> 00:26:21,600
next time you want to go somewhere,

298
00:26:21,680 --> 00:26:25,880
tell Chayanee and me.
I'll take you myself.

299
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:30,600
Thank you for taking care
of Grandpa, Hathaya.

300
00:26:30,680 --> 00:26:33,960
But now that you've
brought him home safely,

301
00:26:34,040 --> 00:26:35,520
you can go back.

302
00:26:36,400 --> 00:26:37,760
I did not just bring him home.

303
00:26:39,840 --> 00:26:42,040
Then why did you come?

304
00:26:46,080 --> 00:26:48,560
Did you miss your husband?

305
00:26:48,640 --> 00:26:50,120
Is that why you came back?

306
00:26:50,200 --> 00:26:51,560
That's right.

307
00:26:52,160 --> 00:26:53,240
Hathaya missed me,

308
00:26:53,880 --> 00:26:55,320
and I missed her too.

309
00:26:56,680 --> 00:26:58,600
I want her to come back and stay here.

310
00:26:59,320 --> 00:27:02,360
Then go be sweet
with each other at your own house.

311
00:27:03,520 --> 00:27:05,360
Take your wife home.

312
00:27:05,440 --> 00:27:06,600
Hathaya is staying here.

313
00:27:08,680 --> 00:27:12,760
I brought Hathaya back to help with
the development. She'll be staying here.

314
00:27:13,560 --> 00:27:16,600
Father, I don't understand.

315
00:27:16,680 --> 00:27:18,400
Why have you changed so much?

316
00:27:18,480 --> 00:27:23,200
I want Hathaya back at work
because I need someone honest.

317
00:27:23,280 --> 00:27:24,800
Not people who steal from me like you.

318
00:27:25,720 --> 00:27:28,480
Father, what are you saying?

319
00:27:29,560 --> 00:27:31,960
I checked those accounts myself.

320
00:27:32,600 --> 00:27:34,520
Did you really think I didn't know
you were embezzling money?

321
00:27:39,400 --> 00:27:42,280
I wanted to know whether Hathaya
would stand by me or by you.

322
00:27:43,600 --> 00:27:45,120
And as for the fire,

323
00:27:45,880 --> 00:27:48,480
the reason I didn't report it
is because I knew perfectly well

324
00:27:48,560 --> 00:27:49,880
that the two of you were involved.

325
00:27:57,200 --> 00:28:00,360
What surprised me was that
Hathaya tried to protect you

326
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:04,400
even though you kept
trying to drive her away.

327
00:28:04,480 --> 00:28:05,800
I don't understand it.

328
00:28:06,440 --> 00:28:09,680
Hathaya has been good to you,
but you respond with pure contempt.

329
00:28:09,760 --> 00:28:11,960
Hathaya came here
and stole Grandpa's love from me.

330
00:28:12,960 --> 00:28:16,280
Before she came,
Grandpa loved and doted on me.

331
00:28:16,360 --> 00:28:18,520
But after Hathaya moved in,

332
00:28:18,600 --> 00:28:21,760
everything she did was suddenly
better than anything I did.

333
00:28:22,560 --> 00:28:25,280
Grandpa gave her a marketing job,

334
00:28:25,360 --> 00:28:28,200
let her sell the houses, and even
had her inspect Mom's accounts.

335
00:28:28,280 --> 00:28:31,200
You're the one who changed, Grandpa.
You don't love me anymore.

336
00:28:31,280 --> 00:28:32,960
You don't love me anymore.

337
00:28:34,840 --> 00:28:37,800
I deliberately turned a blind eye
and didn't report you to the police.

338
00:28:38,600 --> 00:28:40,240
And you still think I don't love you?

339
00:28:47,560 --> 00:28:49,280
If you really love me,

340
00:28:51,160 --> 00:28:53,480
can I ask you for one thing?

341
00:28:54,120 --> 00:28:57,720
Please make Hathaya live somewhere else.
That's all I'm asking.

342
00:29:05,640 --> 00:29:09,000
I feel guilty that your father
died because of me.

343
00:29:10,320 --> 00:29:11,840
And I'm also sorry

344
00:29:13,000 --> 00:29:16,440
I indulged your every wish
until you became selfish,

345
00:29:16,520 --> 00:29:18,720
demanding, and completely spoiled.

346
00:29:20,560 --> 00:29:22,800
If you love me, Grandpa,

347
00:29:22,880 --> 00:29:25,200
can I please ask you

348
00:29:26,320 --> 00:29:30,360
to make Hathaya live somewhere else?
That's all.

349
00:29:35,280 --> 00:29:37,640
I understand how you feel, Chaya.

350
00:29:38,800 --> 00:29:42,040
I won't live here.
I'll just come help Grandpa with work.

351
00:29:42,880 --> 00:29:44,200
I'll stay with Ramil.

352
00:29:46,640 --> 00:29:47,760
You don't need to worry.

353
00:29:49,320 --> 00:29:50,760
I'll take good care of Hathaya.

354
00:29:52,680 --> 00:29:54,840
Thank you, Ramil.

355
00:29:54,920 --> 00:29:57,760
Then we'll excuse ourselves.

356
00:30:02,280 --> 00:30:03,800
Come on, wifey.

357
00:30:14,760 --> 00:30:15,960
Grandpa.

358
00:30:16,480 --> 00:30:18,760
I'm sorry.

359
00:30:18,840 --> 00:30:21,000
Can you give me another chance?

360
00:30:22,280 --> 00:30:23,440
Father.

361
00:30:26,040 --> 00:30:28,200
I'm so sorry.

362
00:30:28,280 --> 00:30:30,520
Please forgive me.

363
00:30:30,600 --> 00:30:34,320
I promise I'll never make you upset again.

364
00:30:37,080 --> 00:30:39,560
All right. Go on. I want to rest.

365
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:05,280
Don't. Hubby will carry it for you, wifey.

366
00:31:06,280 --> 00:31:09,000
Stop talking like that.

367
00:31:09,080 --> 00:31:10,800
It makes my skin crawl.

368
00:31:10,880 --> 00:31:13,800
And don't ever tell anyone I missed you.

369
00:31:14,400 --> 00:31:15,960
I never missed you.

370
00:31:18,040 --> 00:31:19,640
Maybe you didn't miss me…

371
00:31:21,760 --> 00:31:22,800
but I missed you.

372
00:31:32,560 --> 00:31:33,760
I'm kidding.

373
00:31:36,280 --> 00:31:40,360
I have no feelings for you. I just
can't stand that mother-daughter pair.

374
00:31:45,720 --> 00:31:47,480
I'll carry my own things.

375
00:31:47,560 --> 00:31:49,800
Go inside. Papang must be
missing you terribly.

376
00:31:51,120 --> 00:31:53,480
Go. Let go.

377
00:31:53,560 --> 00:31:54,880
You really didn't miss me?

378
00:31:54,960 --> 00:31:57,400
Go already. And stop talking.

379
00:32:14,800 --> 00:32:16,600
Should've let him help.

380
00:32:23,160 --> 00:32:25,440
Papang. Daddy's home.

381
00:32:26,120 --> 00:32:27,240
Papang.

382
00:32:27,800 --> 00:32:29,360
Daddy's back!

383
00:32:29,440 --> 00:32:30,800
Come here.

384
00:32:31,600 --> 00:32:34,880
What do we do first
when we see each other?

385
00:32:34,960 --> 00:32:36,200
Hello, Daddy.

386
00:32:36,280 --> 00:32:37,760
Not enough.

387
00:32:39,240 --> 00:32:41,640
That's my sweet boy.

388
00:32:44,040 --> 00:32:46,760
I brought you some snacks too.

389
00:32:47,600 --> 00:32:48,800
Here.

390
00:32:49,480 --> 00:32:50,320
Thank you.

391
00:32:50,400 --> 00:32:52,920
Wait. What do you
have to do before eating?

392
00:32:53,000 --> 00:32:54,520
-Wash my hands.
-Yes.

393
00:32:54,600 --> 00:32:55,720
Go ahead.

394
00:33:02,360 --> 00:33:04,640
I came to sit with Papang
so Max could go to work.

395
00:33:05,560 --> 00:33:08,400
Now that you're back, I'll head home.

396
00:33:08,480 --> 00:33:11,040
And here. Papang loves this story.

397
00:33:11,120 --> 00:33:13,720
He's heard it a hundred times
and never gets tired of it.

398
00:33:13,800 --> 00:33:15,960
Keep it and read it to him.

399
00:33:22,200 --> 00:33:23,560
I want to talk to you about Papang.

400
00:33:24,160 --> 00:33:26,320
I'm busy, Mom.

401
00:33:27,160 --> 00:33:29,720
Don't waste your time on me.
And you don't need to come here again.

402
00:33:32,360 --> 00:33:33,760
I can take care of Papang myself.

403
00:33:35,640 --> 00:33:38,640
You have to work.
I can help take care of my grandson.

404
00:33:40,600 --> 00:33:44,400
I already told you.
I can take care of Papang myself.

405
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:48,440
He's my son.
I can take responsibility for him.

406
00:33:50,880 --> 00:33:52,760
Papang is my grandson too.

407
00:33:54,400 --> 00:33:55,840
Please let me help take care of him.

408
00:33:59,560 --> 00:34:01,040
-Hello.
-Hello, dear.

409
00:34:06,080 --> 00:34:07,160
Grandma left already?

410
00:34:09,320 --> 00:34:10,440
Yes.

411
00:34:11,040 --> 00:34:14,000
And from now on, let's not bother
Grandma too much, okay?

412
00:34:14,080 --> 00:34:16,159
Grandma tells fun stories.

413
00:34:17,199 --> 00:34:18,639
More fun than that auntie.

414
00:34:21,840 --> 00:34:23,840
I'm going upstairs to put my things away.

415
00:34:27,440 --> 00:34:29,120
And don't bother me.

416
00:34:29,199 --> 00:34:32,040
I'm going to perform a ritual

417
00:34:32,120 --> 00:34:34,800
and cast a spell
to defeat naughty children.

418
00:34:37,560 --> 00:34:39,280
THE FROG PRINCE

419
00:34:39,360 --> 00:34:42,159
Daddy, I'm scared.

420
00:34:50,159 --> 00:34:53,159
Don't be scared. She's only teasing you.

421
00:34:53,239 --> 00:34:55,199
Come on. Let's eat some snacks.

422
00:35:03,280 --> 00:35:04,600
Ma'am.

423
00:35:04,680 --> 00:35:07,560
I brought you some snacks.
They're a specialty from my hometown.

424
00:35:07,640 --> 00:35:09,040
Thank you, dear.

425
00:35:09,120 --> 00:35:10,360
Wow.

426
00:35:10,440 --> 00:35:14,560
You have to take care of this house
and help look after Papang too.

427
00:35:14,640 --> 00:35:15,960
You must be exhausted.

428
00:35:16,720 --> 00:35:18,680
Not at all. It's actually fun.

429
00:35:18,760 --> 00:35:22,120
Sometimes being around children is much
more enjoyable than being around adults.

430
00:35:23,560 --> 00:35:26,760
Especially a certain son of yours.

431
00:35:27,560 --> 00:35:29,000
True.

432
00:35:29,080 --> 00:35:30,280
Don't tell him I said that.

433
00:35:36,920 --> 00:35:38,720
-Hathaya.
-Yes?

434
00:35:38,800 --> 00:35:40,800
I need you to talk to Ramil for me.

435
00:35:40,880 --> 00:35:42,480
Oh.

436
00:35:42,560 --> 00:35:44,480
What is it?

437
00:35:45,480 --> 00:35:46,880
It's about Papang.

438
00:35:50,440 --> 00:35:51,640
Okay.

439
00:36:00,240 --> 00:36:03,160
Then I'll excuse myself. Goodbye.

440
00:36:03,240 --> 00:36:04,320
Bye.

441
00:36:10,000 --> 00:36:11,360
Hello.

442
00:36:18,600 --> 00:36:20,280
What was Ramil's wife doing here?

443
00:36:20,360 --> 00:36:23,640
Hathaya just came back from her hometown,
so she brought me some snacks.

444
00:36:23,720 --> 00:36:26,400
I already told you
not to talk to those people.

445
00:36:26,480 --> 00:36:29,280
Do you understand? And you too.

446
00:36:29,360 --> 00:36:30,720
Don't talk to them.

447
00:36:30,800 --> 00:36:33,640
If Chayanee finds out, she'll get angry.

448
00:36:39,840 --> 00:36:42,280
-Papang has grown so much.
-You don't have to tell me.

449
00:36:43,000 --> 00:36:43,920
I don't want to know.

450
00:36:47,520 --> 00:36:50,320
But the child you're talking
about is your son.

451
00:36:51,080 --> 00:36:55,480
If Dad finds out you're talking to me
about this, he won't be happy.

452
00:37:13,040 --> 00:37:14,120
What are you doing?

453
00:37:16,280 --> 00:37:17,320
Where were you?

454
00:37:18,120 --> 00:37:20,560
I warmed up some food for you.

455
00:37:22,000 --> 00:37:24,560
I stopped by to give
your mother some gifts.

456
00:37:26,560 --> 00:37:29,720
Don't go over there.
They don't want us around.

457
00:37:31,800 --> 00:37:36,120
Your mother really loves Papang
and worries about him.

458
00:37:41,840 --> 00:37:45,040
She told me that while you were away,

459
00:37:45,120 --> 00:37:47,200
Papang kept crying for you.

460
00:37:47,280 --> 00:37:51,440
And when he was asleep,
he called for his mother.

461
00:37:55,920 --> 00:37:59,800
He probably misses Nuchwara.
He must really want to see her.

462
00:38:03,840 --> 00:38:04,840
Go eat.

463
00:38:04,920 --> 00:38:07,320
I'm going to bed.

464
00:38:36,320 --> 00:38:38,040
NUCHWARA

465
00:38:39,400 --> 00:38:40,840
Please leave a message--

466
00:39:01,000 --> 00:39:02,280
Daddy?

467
00:39:06,320 --> 00:39:07,680
Daddy?

468
00:39:08,200 --> 00:39:10,120
Good morning.

469
00:39:10,200 --> 00:39:12,200
Witch. Where's Daddy?

470
00:39:14,520 --> 00:39:16,120
Where could he be?

471
00:39:16,200 --> 00:39:18,120
If you want to know, give me a hug.

472
00:39:19,040 --> 00:39:19,960
Now I don't wanna know.

473
00:39:20,040 --> 00:39:24,680
Why not? Just one hug.
Then I'll tell you where Daddy is.

474
00:39:24,760 --> 00:39:26,080
I'll find him myself.

475
00:39:26,160 --> 00:39:28,400
Come on. Give me a hug

476
00:39:28,480 --> 00:39:31,400
and I'll tell you.

477
00:39:35,280 --> 00:39:37,000
Hello, Nuch.

478
00:39:37,880 --> 00:39:40,600
Why haven't you answered my calls?
How many days has it been?

479
00:39:41,200 --> 00:39:45,440
Your son keeps crying for you, you know?
You can't just abandon him.

480
00:39:45,520 --> 00:39:48,640
Hello? Hello? Nuch?

481
00:39:49,640 --> 00:39:52,280
Mommy abandoned me.

482
00:39:55,440 --> 00:39:57,840
No. Mommy didn't abandon you.

483
00:39:57,920 --> 00:40:00,120
I heard you.

484
00:40:00,200 --> 00:40:02,040
Mommy isn't coming to get me.

485
00:40:02,120 --> 00:40:03,720
Mommy abandoned me.

486
00:40:04,720 --> 00:40:08,320
No. Mommy just has to work.
She'll come back.

487
00:40:09,120 --> 00:40:11,520
Daddy, please don't leave me.

488
00:40:11,600 --> 00:40:14,400
I promise. I'll never leave you.

489
00:40:14,480 --> 00:40:15,640
Come here.

490
00:40:42,360 --> 00:40:43,200
What is it, Max?

491
00:40:44,400 --> 00:40:45,760
What? What happened?

492
00:40:48,200 --> 00:40:49,720
Okay. I'll be there right away.

493
00:40:51,600 --> 00:40:52,880
What happened?

494
00:40:52,960 --> 00:40:56,720
The workers built something incorrectly.
I'll have to go and correct them.

495
00:40:56,800 --> 00:40:59,280
Go. I'll take care of Papang.

496
00:41:02,600 --> 00:41:06,440
But I'm worried that
if he wakes up and I'm gone,

497
00:41:07,040 --> 00:41:08,600
he'll think I abandoned him.

498
00:41:09,240 --> 00:41:10,480
Don't worry.

499
00:41:10,560 --> 00:41:14,640
When he wakes up, I'll video call you
so he can see that you're working.

500
00:41:18,800 --> 00:41:19,640
Look after him.

501
00:41:45,560 --> 00:41:46,840
Still asleep.

502
00:41:48,840 --> 00:41:50,360
I'll go to the market.

503
00:41:52,760 --> 00:41:55,400
I'll buy some things
and make you something to eat.

504
00:42:13,240 --> 00:42:16,160
-How much?
-One hundred baht.

505
00:42:16,960 --> 00:42:18,680
Could you hurry, please?
I need to get home.

506
00:42:31,400 --> 00:42:32,480
Daddy?

507
00:42:34,560 --> 00:42:35,800
Daddy, where are you?

508
00:42:58,480 --> 00:42:59,760
Daddy.

509
00:43:01,000 --> 00:43:02,320
Daddy.

510
00:43:14,600 --> 00:43:15,960
Daddy?

511
00:43:17,560 --> 00:43:19,360
Daddy, where are you?

512
00:43:29,240 --> 00:43:30,520
Daddy?

513
00:43:37,120 --> 00:43:40,440
Daddy, where are you?

514
00:43:41,320 --> 00:43:43,640
There's no one home.

515
00:43:46,680 --> 00:43:49,120
Maybe Daddy went to see Grandma.

516
00:43:57,920 --> 00:43:59,320
Grandma?

517
00:44:05,160 --> 00:44:06,600
Grandpa.

518
00:44:07,200 --> 00:44:08,760
Grandpa.

519
00:44:10,400 --> 00:44:11,520
Grandpa.

520
00:44:12,320 --> 00:44:13,400
What?

521
00:44:13,480 --> 00:44:14,640
Hey.

522
00:44:15,720 --> 00:44:17,000
What are you doing here?

523
00:44:17,080 --> 00:44:21,160
Grandpa, where's Daddy?
I came looking for Daddy.

524
00:44:25,440 --> 00:44:28,000
Uncle, have you seen Daddy?

525
00:44:29,720 --> 00:44:31,240
Papang, come here.

526
00:44:32,520 --> 00:44:35,320
Daddy isn't here. How did you get here?

527
00:44:37,840 --> 00:44:40,200
I'll take you home.

528
00:44:42,520 --> 00:44:43,600
No.

529
00:44:45,000 --> 00:44:48,280
Go upstairs and change.
I'm taking you to meet someone important.

530
00:44:48,360 --> 00:44:51,480
He has a lot of voter support
in the community. Go.

531
00:44:51,560 --> 00:44:53,760
Can I take Papang home first?

532
00:44:53,840 --> 00:44:57,160
No. I'll take him myself. Go.

533
00:45:02,960 --> 00:45:07,200
Grandpa, you're hurting me.

534
00:45:07,280 --> 00:45:09,040
You're hurt?

535
00:45:09,120 --> 00:45:12,480
Stop calling me Grandpa.
I'm not your grandfather.

536
00:45:12,560 --> 00:45:14,640
I want to go home.

537
00:45:14,720 --> 00:45:18,080
Don't you want to know
where your father went?

538
00:45:18,160 --> 00:45:19,600
Where did Daddy go?

539
00:45:19,680 --> 00:45:21,120
Your father is gone.

540
00:45:21,200 --> 00:45:22,480
Where did Daddy go?

541
00:45:22,560 --> 00:45:25,760
He ran as far away from you as he could.
He doesn't want to see you again.

542
00:45:25,840 --> 00:45:27,760
Just like your mother abandoned you.

543
00:45:27,840 --> 00:45:31,200
That's not true. Daddy said
he would never leave me.

544
00:45:31,280 --> 00:45:32,560
Your father

545
00:45:32,640 --> 00:45:34,360
doesn't want to take care of you.

546
00:45:34,440 --> 00:45:37,960
He wants you back with your mother.
He wants you out of his life.

547
00:45:38,040 --> 00:45:39,840
That's not true. I don't believe you.

548
00:45:39,920 --> 00:45:41,840
Everyone hates you.

549
00:45:41,920 --> 00:45:43,480
No one loves you.

550
00:45:43,560 --> 00:45:45,480
Everyone here hates you.

551
00:45:45,560 --> 00:45:47,880
Go away. Go back home.

552
00:45:47,960 --> 00:45:49,240
I hate you, Grandpa.

553
00:45:49,320 --> 00:45:51,920
I hate you too. Go.

554
00:46:01,360 --> 00:46:03,040
You shouldn't have said
those things to him.

555
00:46:03,120 --> 00:46:05,680
He might run away,
just like he threatened to before.

556
00:46:06,280 --> 00:46:08,960
Good. If he does, I don't care
where he goes or whether he dies.

557
00:46:11,000 --> 00:46:12,360
Where are you going?

558
00:46:12,440 --> 00:46:13,680
I'm going to look after Papang.

559
00:46:13,760 --> 00:46:16,880
No. That isn't your responsibility.

560
00:46:16,960 --> 00:46:18,600
Go back inside.

561
00:46:19,880 --> 00:46:21,280
That's an order.

562
00:46:21,360 --> 00:46:22,640
Didn't you hear me?

563
00:46:23,560 --> 00:46:24,600
Go inside.

564
00:47:12,360 --> 00:47:14,200
Daddy…

565
00:47:15,000 --> 00:47:18,800
Daddy.

566
00:47:27,600 --> 00:47:29,000
Papang--

567
00:47:32,960 --> 00:47:34,040
Papang?

568
00:47:39,440 --> 00:47:40,640
Papang?

569
00:47:41,800 --> 00:47:42,640
Papang.

570
00:47:51,480 --> 00:47:52,760
Papang?

571
00:47:57,600 --> 00:47:58,640
Papang.

572
00:48:00,880 --> 00:48:01,880
Papang.

573
00:48:02,640 --> 00:48:05,440
Papang. Papang.

574
00:48:08,120 --> 00:48:11,160
Ma'am, did Papang come here?

575
00:48:12,080 --> 00:48:15,760
Yes. He came looking for Ramil,
but he already left.

576
00:48:16,880 --> 00:48:20,560
-Why?
-He's not at home.

577
00:48:20,640 --> 00:48:23,120
I'm afraid he may have run away
like he threatened to before.

578
00:48:24,960 --> 00:48:28,400
Then I'll come with you.
We'll look for him together.

579
00:48:29,720 --> 00:48:30,800
Auntie.

580
00:48:33,200 --> 00:48:34,360
Where are you going?

581
00:48:35,280 --> 00:48:36,560
I'm going to look for Papang.

582
00:48:36,640 --> 00:48:40,240
Dad told you not to. I'm only warning you

583
00:48:41,000 --> 00:48:43,240
because I don't want you
getting in trouble.

584
00:48:44,600 --> 00:48:48,760
I know your father will be angry
and that I may get in trouble.

585
00:48:50,080 --> 00:48:51,920
But I can't just stand here

586
00:48:52,000 --> 00:48:56,400
and do nothing when a child is running
away from home with a broken heart.

587
00:49:00,360 --> 00:49:02,560
And what about you? You're his father.

588
00:49:03,280 --> 00:49:04,640
Don't you feel anything at all?

589
00:49:18,120 --> 00:49:19,160
-Help me. Help.
-Quiet!

590
00:49:19,240 --> 00:49:22,120
NEXT EPISODE

591
00:49:22,840 --> 00:49:24,240
That was only a warning shot.

592
00:49:24,320 --> 00:49:26,080
This time, I'll shoot for real.

593
00:49:29,240 --> 00:49:31,320
I helped bring in customers.

594
00:49:31,400 --> 00:49:32,720
They're all people I know.

595
00:49:32,800 --> 00:49:34,400
Thank you so much, Uncle.

596
00:49:34,480 --> 00:49:37,080
Why are you thanking me?
I didn't bring those customers for you.

597
00:49:37,160 --> 00:49:38,760
I've told you before

598
00:49:38,840 --> 00:49:40,640
not to lecture me.

599
00:49:40,720 --> 00:49:43,680
I said go upstairs
and pack your clothes. No shame.

600
00:51:34,680 --> 00:51:39,960
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
